            <ArticleTitle>Arm pain in a dentist: pronator syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>61-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 29-year-old pregnant dentist developed acute right forearm pain and associated weakness in her hand. A diagnosis of pronator syndrome was made. A review of the anatomy, pathophysiology, and treatment of pronator syndrome is given. We present this case to alert dentists, both male and female, of an uncommon but definite occupational hazard.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
